{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Growth","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.Growth","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.growth_sqrt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BlochRigidity.growth_sqrt","kind":"theorem","line":8,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/BlochRigidity/Growth.lean#L8-L124","doc":"**Growth lemma (pure inequalities).** A dilation relation\n`Ω(y) = Ω(10y) - Ω(9y/(1-y))/(1-y) + y R(y)` near `0`, with `R` bounded and `Ω` bounded on one\nannulus, forces `|Ω(y)| ≤ C/√|y|`. Both other arguments sit at a larger radius, and the weights\n`1/√10 + 1/(√8·0.99) < 1` make the induction over shells close. ","signatureChunk":0}]}